    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.hues\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nTo have strikethrough work using Treesitter in Markdown files, I have to do:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.api.nvim_set_hl(0, '@markup.strikethrough', { link='@text.strike' })\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\n0.10.1\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n- Install nvim-treesitter\r\n- `require('mini.hues').setup()`\r\n- Open a Markdown file\r\n- Insert: `~~test~~`\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nThe line will have strikethrough applied on it.\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nNo strikethrough.",
